# Branches and security gate

`main` accepts changes only through a pull request. Do not commit or push to `main`.

## Before changing code

1. Start from an up-to-date `main`.
2. Create a branch named `feature/<short-topic>`.
3. Commit only on that branch.

## Before opening a pull request

Run `scripts/security-scan.sh` from the repo root. Do not open a pull request when it fails.

GitHub Actions runs that script as the `test` check, plus CodeQL, on every pull request to `main`. Do not merge unless the user asks.
